## Context

`slides/manuscript/main.md` (Annex C, *Phase B dialogue policy*)
currently says:

> *TERMINAL (sent when remaining budget ≤ 20% of the cap, or when
> three ENCOURAGE replies have not produced a report)*

This phrasing is ambiguous in light of the 0214 implementation
clarification (the post-merge ticket update): the counter is
incremented before the bound check, so the third **no_report
observation** triggers TERMINAL — meaning ENCOURAGE is sent on the
first two no_reports and TERMINAL on the third. The pure no_report
trace is 4 turns total:

1. designed_prompt → no_report (count 0→1) → ENCOURAGE
2. ENCOURAGE → no_report (1→2) → ENCOURAGE
3. ENCOURAGE → no_report (2→3) → TERMINAL
4. TERMINAL → response captured → stop

The current Annex C wording could be read either way ("3 ENCOURAGE
sent, 4th decides" or "2 ENCOURAGE sent, 3rd is TERMINAL"). The
implementation and tests anchor the latter.

## Actions

1. Rewrite the TERMINAL clause to be unambiguous, e.g.:
   *"TERMINAL (sent when remaining budget ≤ 20% of the cap, or after
   three consecutive `no_report` classifications — ENCOURAGE on the
   first two, TERMINAL on the third)"*
2. Optionally add a parenthetical (4-turn trace) for the reader.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] TERMINAL clause phrasing matches the 0214 implementation
      anchor.
- [ ] No reader can interpret it as "send 3 ENCOURAGE, decide on
      4th."
